  "text": "𐤕⎓\n\n.All the edges of a cube are connected pairwise in pairs. This forms a tesseract (4-dimensional cube) with 32 edges. The cube has 8 vertices, 12 edges, 6 faces, and 4 diagonals.\n\nWe can calculate the length of the 12 edges of the cube.\n\nBy using the Pythagorean theorem in the following way for 1 side of the cube:\n\n2a + 2b = 13 cm2\n\n= b ∗ c = √2 cm\n\nFor c = 13 cm. You cancel one side and get that the other two sides can be drawn with squares of equal size.\n\nThe length of the edges of the cube with face diagonal links are calculated as follows:\n\nb = 6 √2 cm = √7 cm.\n\nThe 13 cm side forms a right triangle with the half length of the diagonals (1.4 cm) and height (6 cm)\n\nForc = 13 - √13 = √111 - √138 = 6.75 cm and the length of the 32 edges is\n\n12 ∗ 13 + 12 ∗ 13 + 13 ∗ 6.75 = 680 cm.\n\n distances Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{.}.\n\n\\ActiveFormsifferent commands for each die are used.\n\nFor the 6cm sides, it is a 6 curvilinear square with 6 dots spaced mm apart. So 6 ∗ 1 = 12. The 90∘ 90- sided diamonds also work here.\n\nThe area required is 70 square cm. Given that the average area of one side is 15 square cm, we can solve for how many rolls we need. We know there are 15 rolls required on average, so we need to find the length of one roll in order to determine the total distance of all of the rolls put together.\n\nTo do this, we must divide the total area required (70 square cm) by the average area of one curve . Given that 132 sides cover the flattened track, one curve can be formed in the track by multiplying these curves to create one curved curve.\n\n.E.println",
